<p>Book IX of Caspar Schott's <em>Technica curiosa</em> (Würzburg 1664) is the first systematic treatment of clockmaking in Europe. Kochański set out the construction of magnetic balances there in cipher, in a work published under another man's name. The key is the number of hours on a dial.</p>
{% include "przyrzady/szyfr.njk" %}
<p class="note uwaga">The shift cipher, the Latin text and the diagram are a reconstruction of the method, not a reading of the original.</p>
